  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">&#x2018;Strengthening land governance for climate resilience: Strategies and lessons from East and Southern Africa&#x2019; - Worldbank Conference session</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This session opens a space to discuss ideas about the effect of climate change on land governance and vice versa, by sharing experiences from Burundi, Uganda, DR Congo, and Mozambique. It is an opportunity for people working in the land governance sector to share their experiences and perspectives on how they are dealing with climate change effects. We will jointly analyze how inclusive land governance can become a crucial tool for improved climate mitigation and resilience, considering the reality and practices of each country.</narrative>
  </description>
